# MyFinance – codebase session guide

Family budget tracker. **Live:** https://myfinance-tau-peach.vercel.app  
Stack: vanilla UI + Vercel serverless API + Supabase Postgres. Product brief: `idea.md`.

## Layout

| Path | Role |
|------|------|
| `public/index.html` | Shell: header, month nav, CSV button, balance card, tabs, modals |
| `public/script.js` | All UI logic: load month, CRUD, colors, CSV export |
| `public/style.css` | Mobile-first styles; paid green / unpaid red; CSV remind pulse |
| `api/incomes.js` | CRUD incomes (scoped by year+month) |
| `api/fixed-expenses.js` | CRUD fixed bills |
| `api/daily-expenses.js` | CRUD daily spend |
| `api/month.js` | `POST` — copy incomes+fixed from prior month into empty month |
| `lib/db.js` | `pg` Pool via `DATABASE_URL` + SSL |
| `lib/http.js` | `send`, `readBody`, `parseYearMonth` |
| `server.js` | Local: serves `public/` + mounts `/api/*` |
| `scripts/init-db.js` | Create/migrate tables (`year`,`month`), indexes, seed |
| `vercel.json` | Rewrites `/` → `public/index.html` (and css/js) |

## Data model

Tables: `incomes`, `fixed_expenses`, `daily_expenses`.  
Every row has **`year`** + **`month`**. UI always queries with current `viewYear` / `viewMonth`.

Fixed payment UX: `is_paid` true → amount **green**; false → **red**.

## Request flow

1. Browser opens site → `loadAll()`  
2. `POST /api/month` with `{ year, month }` (bootstrap if empty)  
3. Parallel `GET` incomes / fixed / daily with `?year=&month=`  
4. Mutations send JSON; creates include year+month  

Local: `npm run dev` → `server.js`. Prod: Vercel functions under `api/` + static from rewrites. Env: `DATABASE_URL` (Session pooler).

## Conventions

- Do not commit `.env` / `.env.local`  
- Prefer Session pooler over `db.*.supabase.co`  
- After schema changes, run `npm run init-db`  
- Keep handlers CommonJS (`module.exports`) to match `package.json` `"type": "commonjs"`  
- Avoid large refactors; match existing Vietnamese UI copy  

## Commands

```bash
npm run init-db
npm run dev
npx vercel --prod
```
